  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nAn overseas contract worker (OCW) or overseas Filipino worker (OFW) is required to file a Philippine income tax return only for income derived from sources within the Philippines. This is governed by Section 24 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which states that an individual citizen of the Philippines who is working abroad is taxable only on income sourced from within the Philippines.\n\nSpecifically, Section 24(A)(1)(b) of the NIRC provides that an individual citizen of the Philippines residing outside the country, including OCWs, is taxed on income derived from sources within the Philippines. Therefore, if an OCW earns income solely from foreign sources, they are not required to file a Philippine income tax return for that income. \n\nIn summary, the filing requirement hinges on the source of income, with only Philippine-sourced income necessitating a tax return.",
